From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:46:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: describe the
 touchscreen

Enable I2C4 and add the NT36772 at 0x62, with its interrupt on GPIO85 as
EINT8, rising, as the vendor driver requests it.

Name no supplies and no reset line. The vendor's chip driver manages
neither, and its resume path needs the display up first. Firmware leaves
the panel on for the retained console, so the rails are expected to be up.

Enabling the bus sends nothing on it. The driver is a module nothing loads.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts    | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 52aa9ef..4734865 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -234,3 +234,33 @@
 		mediatek,battery-thermal-zone = "battery-thermal";
 	};
 };
+
+&pio {
+	touchscreen_pins: touchscreen-pins {
+		pins-irq {
+			pinmux = <MT6797_GPIO85__FUNC_EINT8>;
+			bias-disable;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * The touch controller. Firmware leaves the I2C4 pads muxed and the vendor
+ * sets no state for them, so neither does this node. The vendor driver drives
+ * no supply and no reset line, and needs the display up first, so its rails
+ * are taken to be the panel's and GPIO68 stays unclaimed. Only the module
+ * talks to the controller, and nothing loads the module.
+ */
+&i2c4 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	touchscreen@62 {
+		compatible = "novatek,nt36772-ts";
+		reg = <0x62>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&touchscreen_pins>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&pio>;
+		interrupts = <8 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+	};
+};
